<Layout title="Permanent Disability Lawyer | Barcelona, Spain" description="English-language legal advice in Barcelona on permanent disability and incapacity in Spain: Social Security grades, INSS decisions and employment consequences after the 2025 reform.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Permanent disability / incapacity" title="Permanent disability in Spain can affect both your benefit and your job. Review both." description="The Social Security system recognises different grades of permanent incapacity. The employment consequences also need to be reviewed, especially under the changes introduced in 2025." primaryLabel="Discuss my case" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Sick leave guidance" secondaryHref="/en/employment/temporary-sickness-leave" note="The grade, the decision date and the employment consequences should be reviewed from the actual resolution." />
<section class="section section-paper"><div class="container cards">
<div class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Partial</span><h2>Partial permanent incapacity</h2><p>A relevant reduction in performance for the usual occupation without preventing its fundamental tasks.</p></div></div>
<div class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Usual occupation</span><h2>Total permanent incapacity</h2><p>Prevents the worker from performing the usual occupation, while another occupation may remain possible.</p></div></div>
<div class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">All work</span><h2>Absolute permanent incapacity</h2><p>Prevents the worker from carrying out any profession or occupation.</p></div></div>
<div class="card"><div><span class="card-kicker">Daily assistance</span><h2>Severe incapacity</h2><p>Applies where the person needs assistance from another person for essential acts of daily life.</p></div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">What changed in 2025</span><h2>A permanent-incapacity decision does not automatically mean the employment contract ends.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p><strong>Law 2/2025</strong> changed the Workers’ Statute so that, in certain cases involving total, absolute or severe permanent incapacity, termination is no longer automatic. The process is linked to the worker’s wishes and to whether reasonable workplace adjustments or a compatible vacant position are possible.</p><p>The worker has <strong>10 calendar days</strong> from notification of the relevant decision to state in writing that they wish to continue the employment relationship. The employer has up to <strong>three months</strong> to make the reasonable adjustments or change of post, or, where the legal conditions are met, to adopt a reasoned termination.</p><p><a href="https://www.boe.es/eli/es/l/2025/04/29/2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Law 2/2025 at the BOE →</a></p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-paper"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">What should be reviewed?</span><h2>The grade is only one part of the picture.</h2></div><div class="prose"><ul><li>Your usual occupation and its essential tasks.</li><li>The exact Social Security or INSS decision.</li><li>The grade recognised and the benefit framework that follows from it.</li><li>The notification date.</li><li>Possible workplace adjustments or a compatible alternative position.</li><li>Any subsequent communication from the employer.</li></ul><p><a href="https://www.seg-social.es/wps/portal/wss/internet/InformacionUtil/44539/45982/45983" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check the official Social Security information on permanent incapacity →</a></p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>Could the decision need to be challenged?</h2><p>That depends on the decision itself, the grade recognised, your professional situation and the applicable procedural deadlines. An early review helps identify which document has been issued and which route needs to be studied.</p><p>You do not need to send medical records or ID documents in your first message. Start with the date of the decision and the employment problem you need to resolve.</p></div></section>
<CTA title="Have you been granted permanent disability and are unsure what happens to your job?" text="Tell us the grade recognised, the notification date and what your employer has told you." label="Contact the firm" />
